**Definition (`codePair`).** The coding function code pair assigns its finite list, expression, pair, or tagged value a natural-number index by pairing and list coding.

**Definition (`chainDec`).** A decoded finite list is an admissible fixed-point chain when its first member is the bottom code and each later member is included in the image of its predecessor.

**Definition (`fixPStep`).** The state transformer fix pstep performs one stage of the finite numerical computation encoded in its state.

**Definition (`fixStp`).** One fixed-point search step updates the accumulated chain code and current candidate according to the inclusion characteristic.

**Definition (`fixChainChar`).** The numerical characteristic function fix chain char encodes its Boolean or relational test by zero and one.

**Definition (`gLastOf`).** The last element of a nonempty coded chain is returned, with zero used for the empty chain.

**Definition (`gStepsOK`).** The state transformer g steps ok performs one stage of the finite numerical computation encoded in its state.

